data: {"id":"chatcmpl_ce9afb14-7b21-4cf2-8614-e7ce66993416","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1792097356,"model":"oracle/chrono-chatgpt-pro-pool","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"Referee assessmentC1 is well-posed but known_false. The inequality permits  $|X|=|Y|$ , and the established finite-cardinality correspondence says that equal-size finite sets admit bijections. Such maps do not identify distinct inputs. Thus the equality case is a mathematical obstruction, not an unresolved case of the pigeonhole principle. Lean CommunityNo PDF was available among the conversation’s attachments. This assessment therefore concerns the complete inline statement C1 and the supplied diagnostic excerpts; it does not certify correspondence with an unseen manuscript.Definitions, quantifiers, and the known baselineThe assertion unambiguously means\n$$\\forall\\,X,Y\\text{ nonempty and finite},\\quad\n|Y|\\le |X|\n\\ \\Longrightarrow\\\n\\forall h:X\\to Y,\\ \\exists x,x'\\in X:\nx\\ne x'\\ \\land\\ h(x)=h(x').$$\nThe colliding pair may depend on  $h$ . There is no restriction excluding injective or bijective functions, and nonemptiness does not exclude singleton sets.The standard pigeonhole theorem has the strict hypothesis  $|Y|\u003c|X|$ . The opened Mathlib declaration states precisely that hypothesis and precisely the requested collision conclusion. The independently opened textbook section gives the corresponding noninjectivity formulation in Proposition 1.5.8. Neither supports replacing the strict inequality by a non-strict one. Lean Community+1The distinction also survives the generalized non-strict pigeonhole principle: a bound  $|Y|n\\le |X|$  guarantees a fiber containing at least  $n$  inputs. Substituting  $n=1$  gives a nonempty fiber, not a fiber containing two distinct inputs. leanprover-community.github.ioSeparate methodological judgmentsProof correctness remains not_checked, because this is a statement-only submission. That label does not override the negative truth-status assessment.For the exact C1, escape is undetermined, with null proof shape and no live witnesses. The false equality extension must not receive new-content credit merely because it is stronger than a known theorem. Conversely, C1 must not be labeled bind_only by silently correcting its hypothesis. The corrected strict version would require only instantiation and notation normalization relative to the opened pigeonhole theorem. Lean CommunityThe six supplied diagnostic excerpts concern different assertions. Their coding and decision-tree results discuss identification and cardinality bounds; the remaining results concern word complexity, arithmetic reductions, or factorization through functions. They do not supply C1’s universal collision conclusion under the stated non-strict hypothesis. Their receipt metadata is not treated as independent verification.The affirmative general-theorem utility is unsupported because the assertion is false, not because pure mathematics needs an external application. No information-gain measurement is justified, and no named open-problem settlement is claimed.My recommendation is to reject the present formulation for display as an open conjecture. Replacing  $\\le$  by  $\u003c$  repairs it, but yields a standard known theorem rather than a new conjecture. This is referee feedback, not a publication decision. Lean Community+1JSON{\n  \"recommendation\": \"reject\",\n  \"summary\": \"C1 is well-posed but known_false: its non-strict cardinality hypothesis includes equality, where finite sets admit bijections. Replacing ≤ by \u003c yields the standard pigeonhole theorem, not a new open conjecture. No submitted proof was checked.\",\n  \"strengths\": [\n    \"The finite-set objects, function domain and codomain, and collision conclusion are clearly specified.\",\n    \"The quantifier order is unambiguous and permits a precise comparison with existing pigeonhole theorems.\"\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": [\n    \"The equality case is included in the hypothesis and invalidates the universal collision assertion.\",\n    \"A comparison with the strict pigeonhole theorem must not silently change the submitted hypothesis.\",\n    \"The supplied diagnostic candidate excerpts do not establish entailment, proof escape, or a mathematical contribution for C1.\"\n  ],\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"C1\",\n      \"correctness\": \"not_checked\",\n      \"shape\": null,\n      \"witnesses\": [],\n      \"known\": [\n        \"Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Pigeonhole [opened: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Data/Fintype/Pigeonhole.html]\",\n        \"Mathlib.Data.Fintype.EquivFin [opened: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Data/Fintype/EquivFin.html]\",\n        \"Mathlib.Combinatorics.Pigeonhole [opened: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Combinatorics/Pigeonhole.html]\",\n        \"Proofs about Discrete Structures [opened: https://discrete.openmathbooks.org/dmoi4/sec_logic-structures.html]\"\n      ],\n      \"note\": \"Truth status, proof correctness, escape, information gain, and utility are assessed separately. C1 is known_false, while proof correctness is not_checked because no proof is submitted. Escape for the exact assertion is undetermined; the strict-hypothesis repair would be bind_only relative to the inspected baseline. Affirmative general-theorem utility is unsupported. No information-gain model or named settlement is supplied.\",\n      \"conjecture\": {\n        \"well_posed\": true,\n        \"well_posed_reason\": \"X and Y are arbitrary nonempty finite sets, their cardinalities are ordinary finite cardinalities, and h ranges over every total function X→Y. For each such h the conclusion requires two distinct elements of X with equal images. The pair may depend on h. Equality of cardinalities and singleton sets are included; injectivity and bijectivity are not excluded.\",\n        \"status\": \"known_false\",\n        \"status_reason\": \"The permitted case |X|=|Y| admits bijections by the opened finite-cardinality correspondence. Bijections have no collision between distinct inputs. The strict pigeonhole theorem therefore does not establish C1.\",\n        \"named_works\": [\n          \"Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Pigeonhole [opened: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Data/Fintype/Pigeonhole.html]\",\n          \"Mathlib.Data.Fintype.EquivFin [opened: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Data/Fintype/EquivFin.html]\",\n          \"Mathlib.Combinatorics.Pigeonhole [opened: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Combinatorics/Pigeonhole.html]\",\n          \"Proofs about Discrete Structures [opened: https://discrete.openmathbooks.org/dmoi4/sec_logic-structures.html]\"\n        ],\n        \"escape\": \"undetermined\",\n        \"escape_reason\": \"There is no affirmative proof to assess, and the exact assertion is false. Its unsupported equality extension is not evidence of new mathematical content. Labeling C1 bind_only by applying the strict pigeonhole theorem would change a hypothesis. Only the explicitly corrected strict version is a direct binding of the inspected theorem.\",\n        \"suggestions\": [\n          \"Replace |Y|≤|X| by |Y|\u003c|X| and present the resulting assertion as the standard pigeonhole theorem rather than an open conjecture.\",\n          \"Discuss the equality boundary separately, explicitly noting that bijections are permitted and that nonemptiness does not remove this obstruction.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"methodology\": {\n        \"baseline\": [\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"X and Y are nonempty finite sets with |Y|≤|X|, and h is an arbitrary total function X→Y.\",\n            \"location\": \"CONFIRMED STATEMENTS[0].statement, C1, hypothesis and function quantifier; repeated in SOURCE CONTEXT.\",\n            \"source\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"For finite types A and B, every function f:A→B has distinct inputs with equal images whenever |B|\u003c|A|.\",\n            \"location\": \"Fintype.exists_ne_map_eq_of_card_lt.\",\n            \"source\": \"Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Pigeonhole [opened: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Data/Fintype/Pigeonhole.html]\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"For finite types A and B, |A|=|B| if and only if there exists an equivalence, hence a bijection, between A and B.\",\n            \"location\": \"Fintype.card_eq; F"},"finish_reason":null}]}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl_ce9afb14-7b21-4cf2-8614-e7ce66993416","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1792097356,"model":"oracle/chrono-chatgpt-pro-pool","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"intype.equivOfCardEq.\",\n            \"source\": \"Mathlib.Data.Fintype.EquivFin [opened: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Data/Fintype/EquivFin.html]\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"For finite sets s and t, with t nonempty, a function f mapping s into t, and n a natural number, |t|·n≤|s| implies that some y in t has at least n preimages in s.\",\n            \"location\": \"Finset.exists_le_card_fiber_of_mul_le_card_of_maps_to.\",\n            \"source\": \"Mathlib.Combinatorics.Pigeonhole [opened: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Combinatorics/Pigeonhole.html]\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"For finite sets A and B and a function f:A→B, |A|\u003e|B| implies that f is not injective.\",\n            \"location\": \"Section 1.5, Proposition 1.5.8.\",\n            \"source\": \"Proofs about Discrete Structures [opened: https://discrete.openmathbooks.org/dmoi4/sec_logic-structures.html]\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"searched\": [\n          \"Listed current-conversation files to locate the requested PDF; the tool returned no attached files.\",\n          \"Web queries: 'site.leanprover-community.github.io mathlib pigeonhole exists_ne_map_eq_of_card_lt' and 'site.leanprover-community.github.io mathlib Fintype card_eq exists bijective'. Initial results were poorly targeted and were not treated as absence or novelty evidence.\",\n          \"Web query: 'pigeonhole principle finite sets injective equal cardinality', restricted to math.mit.edu, courses.csail.mit.edu, and discrete.openmathbooks.org. Opened the author-hosted HTML section containing Proposition 1.5.8.\",\n          \"Directly navigated the official Mathlib HTML documentation and performed page-local declaration searches. Opened the strict finite pigeonhole declaration, the equal-cardinality equivalence declarations, and the generalized non-strict fiber bound recorded in baseline.\",\n          \"Compared all six user-supplied diagnostic source_excerpt entries at statement level: binary target identification, word-complexity refutation, exceptional prime ideals, decision-tree cardinality bounds, integer residue classification, and quotient factorization. Did not independently authenticate their frozen identities or execute their code.\",\n          \"Scope was elementary finite-set cardinality, injectivity, bijections, and strict versus non-strict pigeonhole hypotheses. No exhaustive literature or publication-priority search was performed.\"\n        ],\n        \"literature\": \"supported\",\n        \"binding_analysis\": \"Substitution A=X, B=Y, f=h into the strict pigeonhole baseline yields exactly the requested collision conclusion only under |Y|\u003c|X|. Expanding noninjectivity into the existence of distinct equal-image inputs is logical normalization. In the non-strict fiber theorem, n=1 yields only a fiber of size at least one. Projection and recombination do not turn that into size at least two or turn ≤ into \u003c. The equality baseline instead permits bijections. The diagnostic decision-tree cardinality bound permits equality and is not a collision theorem. No manuscript-local proof, helper, alias, wrapper, or tactic expansion was supplied to inline.\",\n        \"delta\": \"Beyond the known strict case, C1 would require: for every pair of nonempty finite sets X,Y with |X|=|Y|, every function h:X→Y has distinct equal-image inputs. This conditional extra obligation conflicts with the opened bijection baseline; it is not an unresolved research gap.\",\n        \"escape\": \"undetermined\",\n        \"witnesses\": [],\n        \"utility\": {\n          \"kind\": \"general_theorem\",\n          \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The submitted affirmative assertion cannot serve as a valid general theorem. This negative finding concerns its truth, not a demand for an artificial downstream application. The referee's status diagnosis is not a submitted counterexample result and is not credited as separate counterexample utility.\",\n          \"problem\": \"Does |Y|≤|X| force every function h:X→Y to have a collision for all nonempty finite sets X,Y?\",\n          \"progress\": \"No affirmative proof is submitted. The inspected baseline identifies a false extension at equality; the strict repair is already known.\",\n          \"prerequisites\": \"Both sets are finite and nonempty; |Y|≤|X| includes equality; h is unrestricted among total functions X→Y.\",\n          \"discharge\": \"The assumptions are explicit, but the universal conclusion is invalid. No valid affirmative discharge or separate computational result is provided.\"\n        },\n        \"settlement\": null,\n        \"information_gain\": null,\n        \"limits\": [\n          \"No attached PDF was available, so manuscript pagination and correspondence with the inline statement are not_checkable.\",\n          \"Correctness is not_checked in the submitted-proof sense; known_false is the separate mathematical status assessment.\",\n          \"Literature support is limited to the inspected elementary baseline, not an exhaustive novelty determination.\",\n          \"Diagnostic receipt identities, freeze labels, and axiom lists were not independently validated and supply no verification credit.\",\n          \"Escape is not inferred from failure of a retrieval query or from the absence of a proof. The false equality extension receives no content credit.\",\n          \"No explicit information-gain model, readout, task, faithful correspondence, or measurement evidence was supplied.\",\n          \"No named open-problem settlement is claimed; confirmed_claims[0].settles is null.\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"knowledge_queries\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"C1\",\n      \"definitions\": [\n        \"X and Y are sets; |X| and |Y| denote their finite cardinalities.\",\n        \"h:X→Y is a total function.\",\n        \"A collision consists of x,x' in X with x≠x' and h(x)=h(x').\"\n      ],\n      \"hypotheses\": [\n        \"X is finite and nonempty.\",\n        \"Y is finite and nonempty.\",\n        \"|Y|≤|X|, including equality.\"\n      ],\n      \"quantifiers\": \"For every pair X,Y satisfying the hypotheses, for every total function h:X→Y, there exist x,x' in X. The pair may depend on X,Y,h. Singleton sets and equal cardinalities are included.\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"There exist x,x' in X such that x≠x' and h(x)=h(x').\",\n      \"search_terms\": [\n        \"pigeonhole principle\",\n        \"Dirichlet box principle\",\n        \"finite-set collision theorem\",\n        \"Fintype.exists_ne_map_eq_of_card_lt\",\n        \"injective functions between finite sets\",\n        \"equal cardinality and bijections\",\n        \"Fintype.card_eq\",\n        \"Fintype.equivOfCardEq\",\n        \"strict versus non-strict cardinal inequality\",\n        \"singleton equality boundary\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"Retrieve exact source statements addressing the non-strict hypothesis, comparing strict pigeonhole results with equal-cardinality bijection results without changing C1. Preserve singleton and equality cases. This is one proposed semantic query for subsequent execution, not a completed knowledge-index search or a claim of formal entailment.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"limits\": [\n    \"The assessment is restricted to the confirmed inline C1 and supplied source excerpts because no conversation PDF was available.\",\n    \"Opened sources are model-reported references, not venue-verified references.\",\n    \"No submitted proof was checked, no proof or research attack is supplied, and no live proof-escape witnesses are claimed.\",\n    \"The negative truth finding is distinct from unavailable manuscript evidence and from the undetermined proof-escape classification.\",\n    \"The supplied diagnostic search was truncated; its metadata and no-match information do not establish novelty or entailment.\",\n    \"No Lean compilation, Trureturing registration, AURIC/FIB measurement, combined score, or escape percentage is claimed.\",\n    \"The root knowledge query is a proposal for the subsequent source audit, not an already-executed query.\",\n    \"The recommendation is feedback on the present mathematical formulation and does not decide publication.\"\n  ],\n  \"text\": \"Do not display C1 as an open conjecture in its current form. Corr"},"finish_reason":null}]}

